e query call pair:\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:1:# DaoJing DHT: Content-Addressed Segment Distribution\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:3:Status: **contract frozen 2026-09-30 (DHT epic slice S0); S1 through S5 are\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:5:plain Clojure path S5 added. Subordinate to\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:10:## 1. Overview and scope\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:29:hashes to the address, a fetching node verifies what a peer hands it against\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:32:Nothing at this layer knows or records which stream, agent, or peer carried a\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:36:only a peer address cannot learn which manifest is current. A restart reads\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:40:## 2. Layering and composition\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:52:or clock, on any host.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:63:| `:traffic` + cursor, `:datagrams` | Reader on the socket's raw traffic stream and its writer handle. **Both absent in solo mode.** |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:65:| `:dao.jing.dht/secret` | Root secret bytes for cookies (section 8). Absent in solo mode; required with a socket from S4. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:66:| `:dao.jing.dht/bootstrap` | Contacts `[{:host ip-literal :port p} ...]`: unproven candidates, nothing more. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:67:| `:dao.jing.dht/publish?` | Publication declaration, default `false` (section 4.4). |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:68:| `:dao.jing.dht/ack-peers` | Peers a write must be sent to before it is acknowledged. Default 2, floor 2, ceiling `k` (section 4). |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:70:| `:dao.jing.dht/bind-host` | Local socket bind IP literal for rejecting opposite-family peer destinations before appending a datagram. Defaults to `127.0.0.1` in loopback S3. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:73:throws on a composition defect (an `ack-peers` below 2 or above `k`, a missing\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:83:and 4.5 say. Configuring peers later is a new composition.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:87:1. Drain `:ticks` to `blocked`; the newest reading is `now`.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:100:## 3. The stream API\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:107:blocking, host policy), `dao.jing.content.async` (callback facade). No DHT\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:138:| `:dao.jing.dht/sent` | `/address`, `/peers n` | **The acknowledgement.** Every datagram of the write was handed to the socket toward `n` distinct peers, `n >= ack-peers`. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:139:| `:dao.jing.dht/unacknowledged` | `/address`, `/reason`, `/peers m`, `/local` | The write is not acknowledged. `m < ack-peers` is how many peers it was sent to; `/local` is the local verdict or `nil`. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:140:| `:dao.jing.dht/replicated` | `/address`, `/peers n`, `/confirmed c` | Replication after the acknowledgement has finished. `c` peers replied that they stored it. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:141:| `:dao.jing.dht/miss` | `/address`, `/reason` | A get ended not found: `/exhausted`, `/deadline`, `/solo`, `/busy`. |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:147:## 4. Writes: local insert, then acknowledged when sent to multiple peers\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:151:works because the data is written to a peer\"; \"sent to a peer but it must send\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:152:to multiple peers before it can be considered ack\"; local copy: \"Yes, local +\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:155:### 4.1 What the acknowledgement asserts\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:159:`ack-peers` distinct peers.**\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:163:  the message, chunks included. A peer for which any datagram answered\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:165:- A peer counts only if it is a **proven** routing entry (section 6) that is\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:168:  carried the cookie the store uses (section 8). A peer that is not fresh is\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:170:- The acknowledgement says **sent to N peers**. It never says stored by N\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:171:  peers, received by N peers, or durable anywhere but locally. The word\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:173:  peers' own replies, which are claims.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:174:- `ack-peers` is composition data: default 2, floor 2, ceiling `k`. One peer\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:179:### 4.2 Two entry points, one pending write\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:193:the address, the request ids waiting on it, the peers sent to, and its\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:196:### 4.3 How a write proceeds, and what the caller sees when it cannot\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:202:2. **Send** the store message to fresh candidates, nearest first, until `ack-peers` are counted. With a warm table this happens in the\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:204:3. **Too few known peers** (a cold bootstrap, a small table): the write starts\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:206:   proven peer is sent to as it appears.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:207:4. **Acknowledge** the moment the count reaches `ack-peers`: append the\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:210:   send to the `k` nearest peers not already sent to, so that a reader's\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:214:If the count has not reached `ack-peers` when `ack-ticks` have elapsed since\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:223:| `:dao.jing.dht/solo` | No socket is composed. Answered in the step that reads the request. | No |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:224:| `:dao.jing.dht/unpublished` | `publish?` is false (section 4.4). Answered at once. | No |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:228:| `:dao.jing.dht/too-few-peers` | The deadline passed with fewer than `ack-peers` counted. `/peers m` says how many. | Possibly, to `m` |\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:237:`/oversize` answer, no local insert), in every mode including solo. A segment\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:241:one ring append. A round that publishes and reads its manifest back\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:245:### 4.4 Publication (owner decision 1)\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:247:Default: never publish. `:dao.jing.dht/publish?` is a separate declaration,\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.