repl/dht_test.cljc:105:;; A dao.stream.datagram host seam over the test mesh\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:120:          :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:127:(defn- peer-node\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:128:  \"A plain DHT node on the mesh at `port`, publishing, as a map\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:194:      (is (= {:peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 7001}\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:195:                      {:host \"::1\" :port 7002}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:205:    (testing \"the bind host defaults to loopback; any other is explicit\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:206:      (is (= \"127.0.0.1\" (:bind-host (spec [\"--dht-peer\" \"127.0.0.1:7001\"]))))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:207:      (is (= \"0.0.0.0\" (:bind-host (spec [\"--dht-peer\" \"127.0.0.1:7001\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:218:                         [[\"--index-store\" \"dht:d\" \"--dht-peer\" \"localhost:1\"]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:221:                          \"host:port\"]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:223:                          \"host:port\"]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:228:                         [[\"--index-store\" \"dht:d\" \"--dht-bind\" \"localhost\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:251:;; Bullet 1: solo opens no socket; the secret is minted, in memory only\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:266:        (is (nil? (get-in runner [:composition ::dht/secret]))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:267:            \"solo composes no secret: there is nothing to cookie\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:269:            \"the directory is the durable store: lock, HEAD, recovery\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:283:(deftest the-root-secret-is-minted-per-open-in-memory-and-never-persisted\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:292:                                             :peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 1}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:295:            secrets (mapv #(get-in % [:dht :composition ::dht/secret]) shells)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:296:            hexes (mapv dht/bytes->hex secrets)]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:303:          (is (= #{\"content.jing\" \"HEAD\" \"lock\"}\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:304:                 ;; Node's lock is a claim entry, lock.<pid>.<nonce>\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:305:                 (set (map #(if (str/starts-with? % \"lock\") \"lock\" %)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:323:(deftest the-banner-states-what-will-be-shared-before-anything-is\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:324:  (let [banner #(str/join \"\\n\" (main/banner (main/parse-args\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:327:      (let [text (banner [\"--dht-peer\" \"127.0.0.1:7001\" \"--dht-publish\"])]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:332:      (let [text (banner [\"--dht-peer\" \"127.0.0.1:7001\"])]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:336:      (is (str/includes? (banner []) \"solo\")))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:337:    (testing \"the memory store prints no DHT banner\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:338:      (is (empty? (main/banner (main/parse-args [])))))))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:342:;; Bullet 3: per-publication acknowledgement, and no round waits\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:352:                           :peers (mapv (fn [p] {:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port p})\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:360:        peers {21 (peer-node net 21) 22 (peer-node net 22)}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:365:        (testing \"the round completed against :local, before any DHT step\"\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:383:        peers {31 (peer-node net 31) 32 (peer-node net 32)}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:399:(deftest a-publication-short-of-peers-is-reported-with-why-at-the-deadline\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:402:        peers {41 (peer-node net 41)}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:411:        (is (<= 5000 now) \"reported at the ack deadline, not before\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:418:;; Bullet 5: a reader given a manifest address hydrates and queries\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:431:(deftest a-reader-given-a-manifest-hydrates-then-queries-the-remote-index\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:434:        peers {51 (peer-node net 51)}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:444:                         #(line-with % \"hydrated\"))]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:445:          (is (line-with lines (str \"hydrated \" manifest)))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:450:              \"the hydrated index is the reader directory's durable HEAD\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:466:        peers {61 (peer-node net 61)}\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:485:        peers {71 (peer-node net 71)}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:492:                                              :peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 70}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:509:              (do (is (some #{\"3\"} seen) \"evaluated once hydrated\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:510:                  (is (< (index-of seen (line-with seen \"hydrated\"))\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:536:                                             :peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 1}]})})\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:542:            \"nothing is evaluated over a node that never bound\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:545:        (is (= 1 (main/exit-status state)) \"and the host exits failing\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:552:;; The same path from the prompt: the dao.space.dht host module\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:559:(deftest the-repl-queries-a-remote-index-through-the-same-plain-path\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:566:            plain (space.dht/load-index\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:568:                                     :peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 110}]\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:584:               plain plain\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:592:            (let [expected (space.dht/q plain manifest remote-query)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:603:                  \"the plain path answers the publisher's fact\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:605:                  \"the host function answers exactly what the plain path does\")\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:606:              (space.dht/close! plain)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:610:                  [plain more] (space.dht/step plain now)\ntest/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:612:              (recur pub plain reader (+ now 10)\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.dht-process-test\n     2\t  \"DHT epic S5 across real processes and real loopback sockets\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md section 10): separate `yin.repl.main`\n     4\t   JVMs, each over its own locked `dht:<dir>`, exchange content through\n     5\t   their UDP sockets.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Two fetch-only listeners and one publisher: the publisher's round\n     8\t   prints its result at once and its publication is later reported\n     9\t   acknowledged, sent to 2 peers.  Then a reader handed the manifest\n    10\t   address the publisher printed hydrates the publisher's index over the\n    11\t   network before it evaluates the lines already typed at it, and its `q`\n    12\t   answers the publisher's facts under the publisher's session token.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Real processes wait on sockets, so this test polls their output with\n    15\t   bounded deadlines; the DHT core itself still sees only ticks.\"\n    16\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    17\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    18\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    19\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht])\n    20\t  (:import (java.net DatagramSocket)\n    21\t           (java.util.concurrent TimeUnit)))\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\t(def ^:private startup-ms\n    25\t  \"Bound on one JVM REPL's startup: it loads the whole shell from source.\"\n    26\t  240000)\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(def ^:private exchange-ms\n    30\t  \"Bound on one network outcome once every process is up.\"\n    31\t  60000)\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn- free-udp-port\n    35\t  []\n    36\t  (with-open [s (DatagramSocket. 0)]\n    37\t    (.getLocalPort s)))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- temp-dir\n    41\t  []\n    42\t  (str \"target/test-dht-process-\" (random-uuid)))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- delete-dir!\n    46\t  [dir]\n    47\t  (let [f (io/file dir)]\n    48\t    (when (.isDirectory f)\n    49\t      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)] (.delete child))\n    50\t      (.delete f))))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- jvm-command\n    54\t  \"`yin.repl.main` on a JVM over this test's classpath.\"\n    55\t  []\n    56\t  [(str (System/getProperty \"java.home\") \"/bin/java\")\n    57\t   \"-cp\" (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\")\n    58\t   \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"])\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(def ^:private node-script\n    62\t  \"The Node build of `yin.repl.main` (shadow-cljs build `:yin-repl`).\"\n    63\t  \"target/yin-repl.js\")\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn- spawn-command!\n    67\t  \"Start the process `command`, collecting its merged output lines.\"\n    68\t  [label command]\n    69\t  (let [pb (doto (ProcessBuilder. ^java.util.List command)\n    70\t             (.redirectErrorStream true))\n    71\t        process (.start pb)\n    72\t        lines (atom [])\n    73\t        reader (doto (Thread.\n    74\t                       ^Runnable\n    75\t                       (fn []\n    76\t                         (with-open [r (io/reader (.getInputStream process))]\n    77\t                           (doseq [line (line-seq r)]\n    78\t                             (swap! lines conj line))))\n    79\t                       (str \"dht-process-\" label))\n    80\t                 (.setDaemon true)\n    81\t                 (.start))]\n    82\t    {:label label\n    83\t     :process process\n    84\t     :lines lines\n    85\t     :reader reader\n    86\t     :stdin (io/writer (.getOutputStream process))}))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- spawn!\n    90\t  \"Start one REPL process — `command`, a `yin.repl.main` JVM by default,\n    91\t   then `args`.\"\n    92\t  ([label args] (spawn! label (jvm-command) args))\n    93\t  ([label command args]\n    94\t   (spawn-command! label (into (vec command) args))))\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- type!\n    98\t  [{:keys [stdin]} line]\n    99\t  (.write ^java.io.Writer stdin (str line \"\\n\"))\n   100\t  (.flush ^java.io.Writer stdin))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn- await-line\n   104\t  \"The first output line matching `re`, polling until `ms` pass.\"\n   105\t  [{:keys [lines]} re ms]\n   106\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) ms)]\n   107\t    (loop []\n   108\t      (or (some #(when (re-find re %) %) @lines)\n   109\t          (when (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline)\n   110\t            (Thread/sleep 50)\n   111\t            (recur))))))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn- index-of-match\n   115\t  [{:keys [lines]} re]\n   116\t  (first (keep-indexed (fn [i l] (when (re-find re l) i)) @lines)))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- stop!\n   120\t  [{:keys [process] :as p}]\n   121\t  (try (type! p \"(quit)\") (catch Exception _ nil))\n   122\t  (when-not (.waitFor ^Process process 20 TimeUnit/SECONDS)\n   123\t    (.destroyForcibly ^Process process)\n   124\t    (.waitFor ^Process process 10 TimeUnit/SECONDS)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- transcript\n   128\t  [{:keys [label lines]}]\n   129\t  (str label \":\\n\" (str/join \"\\n\" @lines)))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(def ^:private token-query\n   133\t  (str \"(dao.space.query/q (quote [:find ?s :where [?e :yin/value 4242 ?t ?m]\"\n   134\t       \" [?m :yin.repl/session ?s ?t1 ?m1]]) {:view :history})\"))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(def ^:private remote-query\n   138\t  '[:find ?v :where [?e :yin/value ?v]])\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(deftest separate-jvm-processes-exchange-content-over-loopback\n   142\t  (let [[pa pb pc] (repeatedly 3 free-udp-port)\n   143\t        dirs (vec (repeatedly 6 temp-dir))\n   144\t        peer #(str \"127.0.0.1:\" %)\n   145\t        procs (atom [])]\n   146\t    (try\n   147\t      (let [b (spawn! \"listener-b\" [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 1))\n   148\t                                    \"--dht-port\" (str pb) \"--dht-peer\" (peer pa)])\n   149\t            c (spawn! \"listener-c\" [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 2))\n   150\t                                    \"--dht-port\" (str pc) \"--dht-peer\" (peer pa)])\n   151\t            a (spawn! \"publisher-a\" [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 0))\n   152\t                                     \"--dht-port\" (str pa)\n   153\t                                     \"--dht-peer\" (peer pb) \"--dht-peer\" (peer pc)\n   154\t                                     \"--dht-publish\"])]\n   155\t        (swap! procs into [a b c])\n   156\t        (testing \"every process binds its own loopback socket and says so\"\n   157\t          (doseq [p [a b c]]\n   158\t            (is (await-line p #\"dht: node [0-9a-f]+ listening on 127\\.0\\.0\\.1:\\d+\"\n   159\t                            startup-ms)\n   160\t                (transcript p))))\n   161\t        (testing \"the publisher stated what it would share before sharing\"\n   162\t          (is (await-line a #\"publishing is ON\\. Everything in .*content\\.jing will be shared\"\n   163\t                          1000)\n   164\t              (transcript a))\n   165\t          (is (await-line b #\"fetch-only\" 1000) (transcript b)))\n   166\t        (type! a \"(def answer 4242)\")\n   167\t        (let [published (await-line a #\"dht: published :segment/\\S+ .*acknowledged\"\n   168\t                                    exchange-ms)\n   169\t              manifest (second (re-find #\"dht: published :(segment/\\S+)\"\n   170\t                                        (str published)))]\n   171\t          (testing \"the publication is acknowledged: sent to 2 peers\"\n   172\t            (is (some? published) (transcript a))\n   173\t            (is (re-find #\"— acknowledged: sent to 2 peers\" (str published))\n   174\t                (transcript a)))\n   175\t          (testing \"the round printed its result before the network answered\"\n   176\t            (is (< (index-of-match a #\"^(yin> )*4242$\")\n   177\t                   (index-of-match a #\"dht: published\"))\n   178\t                (transcript a)))\n   179\t          (testing \"the publisher's HEAD names what it announced\"\n   180\t            (is (str/includes? (slurp (str (dirs 0) \"/HEAD\")) (str \":\" manifest))))\n   181\t          (type! a \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n   182\t          (type! a token-query)\n   183\t          (let [own (await-line a #\"#\\{\\[\\\"[0-9a-f-]+\\\"\\]\\}\" exchange-ms)\n   184\t                token (second (re-find #\"\\\"([0-9a-f-]+)\\\"\" (str own)))\n   185\t                d (spawn! \"reader-d\" [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 3))\n   186\t                                      \"--dht-peer\" (peer pa)\n   187\t                                      \"--dht-manifest\" (str \":\" manifest)])]\n   188\t            (swap! procs conj d)\n   189\t            (is (some? token) (transcript a))\n   190\t            ;; Typed before the reader has hydrated: these lines wait in its\n   191\t            ;; input medium until the remote index is installed.\n   192\t            (type! d \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n   193\t            (type! d token-query)\n   194\t            (testing \"the reader hydrates the remote index over the network\"\n   195\t              (is (await-line d (re-pattern (str \"dht: hydrated :\" manifest))\n   196\t                              startup-ms)\n   197\t                  (transcript d)))\n   198\t            (testing \"and q answers the publisher's fact under its token\"\n   199\t              (let [answer (await-line d #\"#\\{\\[\\\"[0-9a-f-]+\\\"\\]\\}\" exchange-ms)]\n   200\t                (is (some? answer) (transcript d))\n   201\t                (is (str/includes? (str answer) (str token)) (transcript d))\n   202\t                (is (< (index-of-match d #\"dht: hydrated\")\n   203\t                       (index-of-match d #\"#\\{\\[\\\"\"))\n   204\t                    \"the typed lines ran only once the index was installed\")))\n   205\t            (testing \"the reader's own rounds continue that index, unshared\"\n   206\t              ;; Its require and q rounds each published over the hydrated\n   207\t              ;; index, so its HEAD has moved past the manifest it fetched,\n   208\t              ;; and publishing is off, so none of it left the process.\n   209\t              (is (await-line d #\"dht: published :segment/\\S+ .*NOT acknowledged: publication is off\"\n   210\t                              exchange-ms)\n   211\t                  (transcript d))\n   212\t              (is (re-find #\"\\{:version 1, :manifest :segment/\"\n   213\t                           (slurp (str (dirs 3) \"/HEAD\")))))\n   214\t            (testing \"plain Clojure in this JVM loads the same index over UDP\"\n   215\t              (let [m (keyword manifest)\n   216\t                    node (dht/load-index\n   217\t                           (dht/join {:dir (dirs 5)\n   218\t                                      :peers [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port pa}]})\n   219\t                           m)\n   220\t                    deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) exchange-ms)\n   221\t                    node (loop [node node]\n   222\t                           (let [[node _] (dht/step node (System/currentTimeMillis))]\n   223\t                             (if (or (not= :loading (:status (dht/load-status node m)))\n   224\t                                     (> (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline))\n   225\t                               node\n   226\t                               (do (Thread/sleep 10) (recur node)))))\n   227\t                    expected (try (dht/q node m remote-query)\n   228\t                                  (finally (dht/close! node)))]\n   229\t                (is (= :loaded (:status (dht/load-status node m))))\n   230\t                (is (contains? (set expected) [4242]))\n   231\t                (testing \"and the reader's host functions answer the same\"\n   232\t                  (type! d \"(require (quote dao.space.dht))\")\n   233\t                  (type! d (str \"(dao.space.dht/load-index :\" manifest \")\"))\n   234\t                  ;; D hydrated this very manifest at startup through the\n   235\t                  ;; same load, so load-index answers :loaded at once.\n   236\t                  (is (await-line d #\"^(yin> )*:loaded$\" exchange-ms)\n   237\t                      (transcript d))\n   238\t                  (type! d (str \"(dao.space.dht/q :\" manifest \" (quote \"\n   239\t                                (pr-str remote-query) \"))\"))\n   240\t                  (is (await-line d (re-pattern\n   241\t                                      (str \"^(yin> )*\"\n   242\t                                           (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote\n   243\t                                             (pr-str expected))\n   244\t                                           \"$\"))\n   245\t                                  exchange-ms)\n   246\t                      (str (pr-str expected) \"\\n\" (transcript d))))))\n   247\t            (testing \"each directory is its own, and each is locked\"\n   248\t              (is (= 4 (count (set (take 4 dirs)))))\n   249\t              (doseq [dir (take 4 dirs)]\n   250\t                (is (.exists (io/file dir \"lock\")) dir)))\n   251\t            (if-not (.exists (io/file node-script))\n   252\t              (println (str \"SKIPPED the JVM-to-Node reader: \" node-script\n   253\t                            \" is absent; build it with `clj -M:cljs -m \"\n   254\t                            \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl`\"))\n   255\t              (let [e (spawn! \"node-reader-e\" [\"node\" node-script]\n   256\t                              [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (dirs 4))\n   257\t                               \"--dht-peer\" (peer pa)\n   258\t                               \"--dht-manifest\" (str \":\" manifest)])]\n   259\t                (swap! procs conj e)\n   260\t                (type! e \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n    70\t  4096)\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(def link-round-budget\n    74\t  \"How many serve-and-run rounds one evaluation drives while its VM waits\n    75\t   on a link (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.3 and 7.2).  A round serves the\n    76\t   interpreter once and runs the VM once; a local content source answers\n    77\t   within a few, so the budget is reached only by a link that stays\n    78\t   `:pending`, which the shell then reports as its own non-blocking state\n    79\t   instead of wedging on.\"\n    80\t  40)\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(def query-row-limit\n    84\t  \"The most rows one `dao.space.query/q` answer may carry: members of a\n    85\t   relation or collection, one for a scalar or tuple.  An answer is a\n    86\t   value the REPL prints whole, so a result past a thousand rows is a\n    87\t   query to narrow rather than one to read; a `def` of ordinary size\n    88\t   projects to tens or hundreds of facts, so every fact of a few\n    89\t   definitions still fits.\"\n    90\t  1000)\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(def query-byte-limit\n    94\t  \"The most canonical CBOR bytes one `dao.space.query/q` answer may\n    95\t   encode to, 256 KiB.  Rows bound the count, not the size: one row can\n    96\t   hold a long string literal.  The byte bound keeps every answer on the\n    97\t   bounded call-out a fixed size, so the medium's retention is bounded by\n    98\t   `query-pair-capacity` times this, 16 MiB.\"\n    99\t  262144)\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(def query-pair-capacity\n   103\t  \"Declared capacity of each medium of the session's query call pair, in\n   104\t   elements.  A VM makes one call at a time and the shell answers it in\n   105\t   the same drive round, so a request and its response each occupy one\n   106\t   element, read before the next is made.  A rollback moves the base\n   107\t   VM's call-out cursor to the newest response\n   108\t   (`yin.repl.query/discard-answers`), so no reader ever falls behind by\n   109\t   more than one call.\"\n   110\t  64)\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(def query-serve-budget\n   114\t  \"Requests one query serve round answers.  A VM parks on one call at a\n   115\t   time, so a round that spends it is answering requests the shell's VM\n   116\t   did not make.\"\n   117\t  64)\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(def query-drive-budget\n   121\t  \"The most `dao.space.query/q` calls one drive answers: one evaluation,\n   122\t   or one re-check of a pending run.  A query is answered in the round\n   123\t   it is asked, so without a bound a program that calls `q` without end\n   124\t   would hold its input round in the drive forever.  Each call re-reads\n   125\t   the published index, so a thousand calls is already a long round; a\n   126\t   program past the bound is stopped with `query-call-limit-text` as its\n   127\t   error and its round rolls back like any failed round.\"\n   128\t  1024)\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(def query-call-limit-text\n   132\t  (str \"the evaluation called dao.space.query/q more than \"\n   133\t       query-drive-budget\n   134\t       \" times and was stopped (:yin.repl.query/call-limit)\"))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(def vm-constructors\n   138\t  \"The evaluators on `yin.vm`: the ast-walker, the linear semantic VM\n   139\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md`), and the nameless de Bruijn stack\n   140\t   and register kernels, each starting with an empty image.\"\n   141\t  {:ast-walker ast-walker/create-vm\n   142\t   :semantic semantic/create-vm\n   143\t   :stack #(stack/create-vm [] %)\n   144\t   :register #(register/create-vm nil %)})\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\t(def vm-labels\n   148\t  {:ast-walker \"ASTWalkerVM\"\n   149\t   :semantic \"SemanticVM\"\n   150\t   :stack \"DebruijnStackVM\"\n   151\t   :register \"DebruijnRegisterVM\"})\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- packet->named-datoms\n   155\t  \"The named `:yin/*` datoms of one expanded tree packet, the input the de\n   156\t   Bruijn resolver reads.\"\n   157\t  [packet]\n   158\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n   159\t    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (macro/packet->row-set packet))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- append-stack-image\n   163\t  \"Attach `image` after the stack image `vm` already holds and start at\n   164\t   its first instruction.  A closure a previous input stored (a `def`)\n   165\t   names a body pc in the earlier image, so that image is kept, not\n   166\t   replaced.  `stack/attach-image` admits the incoming image alone under\n   167\t   the current stamp (the expander and the lowerer are its fresh\n   168\t   producers), relocates and appends it, records its offset-table row,\n   169\t   and keeps `:hash` the canonical H of the whole `:segment`\n   170\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3).  Attaching touches no register, so\n   171\t   starting the input is this function's: `:pc` at the image's row, the\n   172\t   registers a fresh run starts with.  An input whose image is already\n   173\t   held reruns at that row.\"\n   174\t  [vm image]\n   175\t  (let [attached (stack/attach-image vm image vm/stack-contract)]\n   565\t     (if (refused? answer)\n   566\t       {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   567\t       (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer))))))\n   568\t\n   569\t\n   570\t(defn- dht-answer\n   571\t  \"The response to one `dao.space.dht` call, answered from `node` — the\n   572\t   shell's DHT node — by the `dao.space.dht` function the operation\n   573\t   names, and the node after it: `load-index` starts a load and answers\n   574\t   its status at once, never waiting; `load-status` answers the load's\n   575\t   status map; `q` answers `dao.space.dht/q` under `limits`, refused\n   576\t   until the index is loaded.  Answers `[node response]`.\"\n   577\t  [node limits request]\n   578\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   579\t        [manifest & more] (apply2/request-args request)\n   580\t        [node answer]\n   581\t        (cond\n   582\t          (nil? node)\n   583\t          [node (unavailable (str \"the shell has no DHT node; start it with \"\n   584\t                                  \"--index-store dht:<dir> and --dht-peer\"))]\n   585\t\n   586\t          (nil? (encoded-size (apply2/request-args request)))\n   587\t          [node (invalid \"dao.space.dht takes portable Yin data only\")]\n   588\t\n   589\t          (not (jing/segment-address? manifest))\n   590\t          [node (invalid (str \"dao.space.dht expects a manifest address, got \"\n   591\t                              (pr-str manifest)))]\n   592\t\n   593\t          :else\n   594\t          (case (apply2/request-op request)\n   595\t            ::dht-load-index\n   596\t            (let [node (dht/load-index node manifest)]\n   597\t              [node {:ok (:status (dht/load-status node manifest))}])\n   598\t\n   599\t            ::dht-load-status\n   600\t            [node {:ok (dht/load-status node manifest)}]\n   601\t\n   602\t            ::dht-q\n   603\t            (let [status (dht/load-status node manifest)\n   604\t                  [query & inputs] more]\n   605\t              [node (if (= :loaded (:status status))\n   606\t                      (bounded #(apply dht/q node manifest query inputs) limits)\n   607\t                      (refusal ::index-unavailable\n   608\t                               (str \"the index \" manifest \" is not loaded (\"\n   609\t                                    (if status (name (:status status)) \"never asked\")\n   610\t                                    \"); (dao.space.dht/load-index \" manifest\n   611\t                                    \") loads it\")\n   612\t                               nil))])))]\n   613\t    [node (if (refused? answer)\n   614\t            {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   615\t            (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))]))\n   616\t\n   617\t\n   618\t(defn- dht-op?\n   619\t  [request]\n   620\t  (contains? (set (vals dht-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   621\t\n   622\t\n   623\t;; =============================================================================\n   624\t;; The interpreter\n   625\t;; =============================================================================\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"node -p 'process.version + \\\" global crypto=\\\" + \"'!!globalThis.crypto + \" require=\" + typeof require'\"' ; rg -n 'dht|:node|query/serve|:head-fn' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | tail -45; rg -n 'js/require|node:crypto|dgram|secure-random' src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc src/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; sed -n '24,32p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '608,660p' docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"node -p 'process.version + \\\" global crypto=\\\" + \"'!!globalThis.crypto + \" require=\" + typeof require'\"' ; rg -n 'dht|:node|query/serve|:head-fn' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | tail -45; rg -n 'js/require|node:crypto|dgram|secure-random' src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc src/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; sed -n '24,32p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '608,660p' docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md\"","aggregated_output":"v26.1.0 global crypto=true require=function\n22:            [yin.repl.dht :as repl.dht]\n743:   (`:head-fn`, yin.repl.store): every session the store outlives\n762:                                   :after-publish (:head-fn index-store)})\n832:   `{:type :dht :dir dir ...}` is the DHT store (yin.repl.dht): that\n833:   durable directory store with a `dao.jing.dht` node composed over it.\n834:   Its step-owner value is `:dht`, advanced only by `yin.repl.dht/step`\n859:                         (if (= :dht (:type index-store-spec))\n860:                           (repl.dht/open index-store-spec)\n877:        :index-store (repl.dht/without-runner index-store)\n879:        :dht (:dht index-store)\n1304:   query interpreter (`yin.repl.query/serve`) answers from the session's\n1336:                         (query/serve {:pair (:query-pair state)\n1339:                                       :dht (:dht state)\n1348:                                      :dht (:dht answered)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:105:   JVM's, Node's `dgram` (required only when a socket binds, so a browser\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:113:(defn secure-random-bytes\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:212:                                          (secure-random-bytes dht/id-length))\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:217:                                       ::dht/secret (secure-random-bytes\nsrc/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs:2:  \"The Node host seam of docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md 3: one `dgram`\nsrc/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs:25:  \"Bind one dgram socket per the seam contract. `:bind-host` is the local\nsrc/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs:45:        ;; `dgram` is required at bind, not at load, so a browser build\nsrc/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs:48:        socket (.createSocket (js/require \"dgram\") family)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc:174:             (.digest (.update (.createHmac (js/require \"crypto\") \"sha256\" key)\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n\n**S5 — REPL integration.** Depends on S4 and on the durable-store epic (spec,\nHEAD, lock, recovery). Acceptance:\n- Default `mem`; `dht:<dir>` is explicit; with no peers it is solo and opens\n  no socket.\n- Publishing requires its own flag, separate from peers, and the REPL states\n  what will be shared before it shares.\n- The REPL shows per publication whether it is acknowledged (sent to N\n  peers) or not and why; no round waits on the network.\n- Two processes with separate locked directories exchange content.\n- A reader given a manifest address hydrates and queries a remote index.\n\n### The plain Clojure path (S5, owner direction 2026-10-01)\n\nOwner, verbatim: \"plain clojure code should be able to query for code in the\ndht. the yin.repl should use the same path as the clojure repl via\nhost-functions\".\n\n`dao.space.dht` (CLJC; JVM, Node, Dart) is that path. It lives under\n`dao.space` because it joins a `dao.jing.dht` node to `dao.space.index` and\n`dao.space.query`; putting it under `dao.jing` would make the\npayload-agnostic well aware of index structure. It has no `yin.repl`\ndependency.\n\n- `(join opts)` composes a node over `:local` (a `dao.jing` store) or `:dir`\n  (its `content.jing`; this API takes no directory lock, so a caller sharing\n  a directory passes its own locked store as `:local`). Options: `:peers`\n  (none is solo: no socket, no secret), `:publish?` (default false, never\n  implied by peers), `:bind-host` (default `127.0.0.1`), `:bind-port`\n  (default 0), `:max-inbound-bytes` (default 64 MiB), `:bind!` (the host\n  datagram seam; each build's own by default). A node with peers mints its\n  root secret at join: 32 CSPRNG bytes, held only in the node value.\n- `(step node now)` is the node's only advance; `now` is its owner's\n  nondecreasing millisecond reading, appended as a tick. It answers\n  `[node events]`: `:bound`, `:bind-failed`, `:published` (per announced\n  publication: acknowledged with the peers sent to, or not with the reason\n  and peers reached, from the `/sent` and `/unacknowledged` facts),\n  `:publication-unknown`, `:loaded`, `:load-failed`.\n- `(store node)` is the node's byte-store handle (5.1); `(announce! node\n  manifest)` closes the publication its puts made.\n- `(load-index node manifest)` starts a load; `step` walks the index through\n  the local store with `dao.space.index/read-manifest` and fetches each\n  missing blob with a `:jing/get` through `dao.jing.content.step`, until all\n  four covered indexes read back and cover the manifest's count.\n- `(db node manifest)` is `dao.space.query/published-db` over the loaded\n  index (`restored-indexes`); `(q node manifest query & inputs)` is\n  `dao.space.query/q` over its current view.\n\n`yin.repl` composes its `dht:<dir>` store with `join` (over its locked\ndurable store), and its `dao.space.dht` host module answers `load-index`,\n`load-status` and `q` with these functions (`yin.repl.dao.space-index.md`,\n\"DHT store\").\n\nOut of this epic: pinning, garbage collection, availability repair and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-30 20:31:00 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-01 03:31:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**SIGN-OFF WITHHELD.** The implementation provides a genuine `dao.space.dht` API outside `yin.repl`, and the REPL host functions call that API. The code also supports the S5 behavior for an explicitly selected DHT store: `mem` remains the default; solo opens no socket; publication is separately enabled and announced before sharing; publication outcomes come from DHT facts; rounds use the local store; and the process test exercises remote hydration and query over loopback. The secret is minted in memory for each networked join, and the bind default is loopback.\n\n| Severity | File:line | Issue | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| High | [dao.space.dht.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-dht-s5/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:173) | Public `join {:dir …}` opens `content.jing` without the directory lock required by the durable store contract. Two plain callers can open the same directory. | Put a reusable locked directory store under `dao.*` and use it for `:dir`; retain `:local` for callers supplying an already locked store. |\n| Medium | [dht_process_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-dht-s5/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj:247) | Seeing a `lock` file does not prove that concurrent opening is refused. The Node exchange is silently optional when `target/yin-repl.js` is absent (line 251). | Add a competing-open assertion. Make the Node leg a required, built test target if JVM↔Node is claimed as acceptance evidence. |\n| Medium | [dht_process_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-dht-s5/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj:34) | Reserving ports by opening and closing temporary sockets creates a bind race on loaded hosts. | Have listeners bind ephemeral ports and pass their reported addresses to subsequent processes, or retry port collisions. |\n\n**Rulings on the open points:** (a) Refusing bind and port flags in solo mode is coherent with “no peers means solo”; a first node can list peers that are not up yet. It does not create a privileged node. (b) The lock belongs in a reusable `dao.*` host store because `join {:dir …}` is a public plain-Clojure entry point; this is the sign-off blocker. (c) The Node leg is useful evidence when built, but a notice and skip cannot serve as a dependable cross-host gate. (d) The single Dart-client failure followed by a passing rebuild is inconclusive; it is not by itself an S5 finding.\n\nThe lazy `js/require` calls are sound for the stated Node path and allow the browser build to load these namespaces without binding a socket. They do not make networked DHT operation available in a browser. The author reports passing JVM, CLJS, Dart, and build lanes; I inspected their report and code but did not independently rerun those lanes in this read-only review."}}
